 "answer": "I can't pull a live reading, so these are the latest figures the search returned. They come from snapshots taken at different times, and some are old.\n\n- **Weather Underground (Penang):** the AQI was 68, which is **Moderate**, with PM2.5 as the main pollutant. This is modelled data from the Copernicus Atmosphere Monitoring Service.\n- **AccuWeather (Penang International Airport):** the AQI was 67. The page labels this \"Poor\" and says it is unhealthy for sensitive groups, though 67 is normally in the Moderate range.\n- **IQAir:** the stations reported different values.\n  - Bukit Mertajam was 58 (Moderate), with PM2.5 at 12.9 µg/m³.\n  - George Town was 125 (Unhealthy for sensitive groups), but that snapshot looks old.\n  - Tanjung Tokong was 79 (Moderate).\n\n**Summary:** Air quality in Penang is probably **Moderate**, with an AQI of roughly 60–80 and PM2.5 as the main pollutant. It can reach unhealthy levels for sensitive groups at some stations, such as George Town, during haze episodes.\n\n**What to do:** People with asthma, heart or lung conditions, and older adults or young children should limit prolonged heavy exertion outdoors. Most other people can carry on as normal.\n\nFor a true real-time reading, check IQAir, or the Malaysian Department of Environment's MyAQI (airduino/APIMS) at the Penang stations.",
